# Factory security (AI-built apps fail here)

- Never ship `allow read, write: if true`. Default deny, then allow one collection.
- Firestore is document-level, not column RLS. A public read returns every field. Split `public_contacts` vs `nojic_mailboxes`. Never store `forwardTo`, API keys, or personal inboxes on a readable doc.
- Never trust the client: `isPremium`, `isAdmin`, `role`, and IAP status are server/store-owned. Clients cannot write those fields.
- Paywall / entitlement check runs before any paid API (Gemini). UI hiding is not access control.
- No secrets in git, `AppConfig`, or `--dart-define` that you cannot rotate. Gemini in the binary is extractable; prefer a Cloud Function proxy when the key must stay private.
- Do not log emails, photos, or tokens. Do not create user accounts unless the week’s product requires them.
- Storage default deny. Cloud Functions verify `request.auth` (and App Check when added).
- If you add SQL/Supabase later: RLS on, no `USING (true)` for writes, no client-set `is_admin`.
